course: dictionary
lesson: 2731
title: Speaking diplomatically
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diplomatically means in a tactful way. Being tactful means choosing your words carefully, so you do not upset or offend people. Think of it as saying a true thing in a kind way.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Come along in, and have some lunch». It is a warm, friendly invitation. Someone speaking diplomatically picks kind words like these, even when the news is not what the other person wants to hear.
explain: Here is an everyday example. Your friend shows you a drawing you do not like best. You could say, "I prefer the other one", and not hurt them. You are being honest, but you are also being diplomatic.
explain: Diplomacy also means the work of governments talking and agreeing with each other. When countries solve problems diplomatically, they use talks instead of war. So the same word can describe kind words between friends and careful talks between countries.
fact: Diplomatically means in a tactful way, careful not to upset or offend people.
fact: Diplomacy is the work of governments talking and agreeing with each other.
fact: Countries can solve problems diplomatically, through talks instead of war.
fact: The adverb forms are diplomatically, more diplomatically and most diplomatically.
fact: The word comes from diplomatic, and the ending -ly turns it into an adverb that describes how something is done.
exercise: Sam tells his friend kindly that he prefers a different drawing, so his friend does not feel hurt. How is Sam speaking? | *Diplomatically | Loudly | Rudely | Sadly
exercise: What does diplomatically mean? | In a great hurry, without stopping | *In a tactful way, careful not to upset people | Very loudly, so everyone can hear | Bluntly and rudely, saying exactly what you think
exercise: Two countries have a disagreement. They use talks to solve it instead of fighting. How are they solving it? | With a loud shout | Secretly, and never telling anyone | Angrily, by sending soldiers | *Diplomatically
test: Which word means in a tactful way? | Noisily | *Diplomatically | Carelessly | Bluntly
test: Diplomacy is the work of governments. Which is an example of diplomacy? | *Two countries talking to agree on a peace deal | A shopkeeper counting coins | A child sharing toys at playtime | A football match between two schools
exam: Which sentence shows someone speaking diplomatically? | "Your drawing is rubbish." | "Go away, I hate it." | "Whatever, I don't care." | *"I really like the colours, but I think the sky would look nicer in blue."
